---
const alignmentLayers = [
  {
    title: "Values Alignment",
    description: "Two people can work equally hard toward completely different definitions of success.",
    elaboration: "When a franchisee's goals, lifestyle expectations, and long-term purpose match the franchisor's vision, commitment holds through the hard stretches. When they don't, an otherwise capable owner slowly disengages and starts questioning the opportunity."
  },
  {
    title: "Cultural Alignment",
    description: "Culture is not a tagline — it's the daily standard that shapes how people work together.",
    elaboration: "When a franchisor's real operating style — how decisions are made, how problems are handled — matches how franchisees naturally behave, the system reinforces itself. When it doesn't, both sides spend more time managing the relationship than growing the business."
  },
  {
    title: "System Alignment",
    description: "Different stages of franchise growth call for different owner profiles.",
    elaboration: "Decision cadence, support availability, and operational clarity all shift as a system matures. Evaluating fit against your current stage — not an idealized version — is what makes a selection decision predictive rather than aspirational."
  },
  {
    title: "Skills Alignment",
    description: "Running a business and executing a specific franchise model are different skill sets.",
    elaboration: "The capabilities that predict success in your system — team leadership, following operational systems precisely, financial discipline — are measurable when you know what to look for, which makes training targeted from day one."
  },
  {
    title: "Execution Alignment",
    description: "Credentials and interviews describe potential. Execution under real-world pressure reveals truth.",
    elaboration: "Some owners are systematic under stress; others thrive with autonomy. Understanding those patterns before and after launch turns alignment from an abstract concept into coaching that actually moves performance."
  }
];

---

<section class="bg-[#f3f3f3] py-20 md:py-28 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="section-shell space-y-20 md:space-y-28">

    <!-- Alignment Stack -->
    <div>
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Our Methodology</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mt-2">The Franchise Alignment Stack™</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#3b3e47]">
        This is how Zorakle analyzes the match between a prospect and your franchise system — five measurable layers of fit, evaluated together to predict who will actually execute.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10">
        {alignmentLayers.map((layer) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 border-t border-[#d1d4dd] py-10 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.9fr)_minmax(0,1.6fr)] md:gap-12 lg:gap-16 lg:py-12">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#22252a] md:text-3xl font-display">{layer.title}</h3>
            <div>
              <p class="text-lg font-medium leading-snug text-[#22252a]">{layer.description}</p>
              <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-[#3b3e47]">{layer.elaboration}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="border-t border-[#d1d4dd]"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/pricing">Get Started Now</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
